& [PublicAPIBoundary: IR6CoordinationMailboxProjectionPrototype] is the future public API boundary for IR6 implementation
  + [api] is validate_claim_identity_envelope(envelope, authority_basis, policy) returns accepted or coordination fault
  + [api] is build_work_boundary_projection(claim_record, packet_record, claim_set, policy) returns work boundary projection
  + [api] is classify_claim_compatibility(claim_a, claim_b, policy) returns compatibility relation, conflict, or interrupt
  + [api] is project_rendezvous_packet(packet_record, claim_context, policy) returns rendezvous projection
  + [api] is project_mailbox_carrier(message_record, cursor_record, claim_context, policy) returns mailbox carrier projection
  + [api] is classify_mailbox_freshness(mailbox_record, cursor_record, claim_context, policy) returns freshness state or stale projection
  + [api] is review_coordination_conflict(conflict_context, policy) returns proceed, block, interrupt, refresh, release, supersede, invalidate, rebake, human override, or refusal decision
  + [api] is review_human_override(override_record, coordination_context, policy) returns scoped result, rejection, expiration, out-of-scope, SJS route, or completion review route
  + [api] is classify_coordination_action(action_packet, policy) returns route, refusal, or SOP-first interrupt context
  + [api] is validate_generated_coordination_output_path(path, generated_output_policy) returns accepted generated path or refusal
  + [api] is run_coordination_mailbox_fixture(fixture_case, expected_ledger, runner_policy) returns generated fixture comparison report
  + [api_status] is future implementation target only

  = must: make identity, boundary, freshness, conflict, stale, human override, refusal, authority tier, and carrier-only status visible in return values
  = must: avoid APIs named or shaped as live mailbox writer, inbox poller, IRC client, Matrix client, web server, UI renderer, agent dispatch, job control, process control, GPU control, model runtime control, network control, credential access, operations control, or live machine control

